{"id":"1.7.1","doc":"T","title":"Data Hazard","words":3330,"blocks":[{"t":"p","s":[{"n":1,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"When instruction A writes the result to register X (including explicit general-purpose registers and implicit special registers), and instruction B needs to use the same register as an input operand, this case is referred to as that instruction B depends on instruction A."}]},{"n":2,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"If instruction A prepares the result to be written to register X at the end of the SA pipeline stage, and instruction B reads the data in register X at the beginning of the SB pipeline stage, then instruction A must be issued D=max(SA-SB+1, 0) cycles before instruction B."}],"warn":true}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":3,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"If the processor fetches instruction B less than D cycles after instruction A, the processor delays issuing instruction B until D cycles have passed."}]},{"n":4,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The act of a processor delaying an instruction because of pipeline interactions is called an interlock."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":5,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Suppose the SA pipeline stage of instruction A is W and the SB pipeline stage of instruction B is E, instruction B is issued to the pipeline D=max(2-1+1, 0)=2 cycles later than instruction A as shown in Figure 1.7-1."}]}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":6,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"When the output operand of an instruction is designed to be available at the end of a pipeline stage, it means that the operation of the instruction is over."}]},{"n":7,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Usually, instructions that depend on this result data must wait until the output operand is written to the corresponding register before retrieving it from the corresponding register."}],"warn":true}]},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":8,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"The Xtensa processor supports the ”bypass” operation."}]},{"n":9,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"It detects when the input operand of an instruction is generated at which pipeline stage of the instruction and does not need to wait for the data to be written to the register."}]},{"n":10,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"It can directly forward the data from the pipeline stage where it is generated to the stage where it is needed."}]}]},{"t":"fig","src":"images/trm-fig-1_7-1.png","alt":"Figure 1.7-1. Interlock Caused by Instruction Operand Dependency","caption":"Figure 1.7-1. Interlock Caused by Instruction Operand Dependency"},{"t":"p","s":[{"n":11,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Data dependencies between instructions are determined by the dependencies between operands and the pipeline stage at which reads and writes happen."}]},{"n":12,"c":[{"t":"text","v":"Table 1.7-2 lists all operands of the ESP32-S3 extended instructions, including implicit special register write (def) and read (use) pipeline stage information."}]}]},{"t":"table","caption":"Table 1.7-2. Extended Instruction Pipeline Stages","head":[[{"t":"text","v":"Instruction"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Operand Pipeline Stage: Use"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Operand Pipeline Stage: Def"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Special Register Pipeline Stage: Use"}],[{"t":"text","v":"Special Register Pipeline Stage: Def"}]],"rows":[{"n":13,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"EE.ANDQ"}],[{"t":"text","v":"qx 1, qy 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"qa 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"—"}],[{"t":"text","v":"—"}]]},{"n":14,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"EE.BITREV"}],[{"t":"text","v":"ax 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"qa 1, ax 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"FFT_BIT_WIDTH 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"—"}]]},{"n":15,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"EE.CLR_BIT_GPIO_OUT"}],[{"t":"text","v":"—"}],[{"t":"text","v":"—"}],[{"t":"text","v":"GPIO_OUT 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"GPIO_OUT 1"}]]},{"n":16,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"EE.CMUL.S16"}],[{"t":"text","v":"qx 1, qy 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"qz 2"}],[{"t":"text","v":"SAR 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"—"}]]},{"n":17,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"EE.CMUL.S16.LD.INCP"}],[{"t":"text","v":"as 1, qx 1, qy 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"qu 2, as 1, qz 2"}],[{"t":"text","v":"SAR 1"}],[{"t":"text","v":"—"}]]},{"n":18,"c":[[{"t":"text","v":"EE.CMUL.S16.ST.INCP